    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49412" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tŭmultŭātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		tumultuor. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A bustling</i>, <i>hurrying</i>, <i>bustle</i>, <i>confusion</i>, <i>tumult</i> (very rare), <i><span class="en">Liv. 38, 2,
				8</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The irregular swearing of the</i> milites
			tumultuarii, acc. to <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 9, 3,
			55</span></i>.</div>
